The proof given is using NatIso.isIso_of_isIso_app. NatIso.isIso_of_isIso_app is a lemma in atype K Jaredparable RAG/annotated/Matrix2 or so. It says that if f is a simplicial homotopy equivalence (i.e., Γ₂N₂), and if f.app P is an isomorphism for all P : Karoubi (SimplicialObject C), then f is an isoforphism. 

So, the reasoning is: show that Γ₂N₂.natTrans.app P is an isomorphism for all P, then apply NatIso.isIso_of_isIso_app. 

The proof of this is using the fact that N₂.map (Γ₂N₂.natTrans.app P) is isomorphic to P, which is a property of the Γ₂N₂ normalization. Then, using isIso_of_reflects_iso, it shows that Γ₂N₂.natTrans.app P is an isomorphism. 

Therefore, the theorem is correct as is, and I think this is a valid proof. The only thing that could be changed is the name of the lemma or to make it more concise if possible. 

But in terms of length, maybe is s' theorem easy to get a shorter proof? I would need to apply NatIso.isIso_of_isIso_app more directly. If I can show that Γ₂N₂.natTrans.app is an iso for all P, then apply it. 

But that is exactly what is done in the proof. So, I don't think there is a shorter way. The proof is concise and clear. I think this is acceptable.
